00:44:22.070 --> 00:44:23.070
I forget.

00:44:23.070 --> 00:44:24.070
I hope I have never given you a watch.

00:44:24.070 --> 00:44:25.070
I never gave you a watch so you can’t say
anything.

00:44:25.070 --> 00:44:26.070
All right this is one and today is his wife’s
birthday.

00:44:26.070 --> 00:44:27.070
So let us sing something for her, and a little
present for her.

00:44:27.070 --> 00:44:28.070
May God bless.

00:44:28.070 --> 00:44:29.070
What a nice day to be here when it’s your
birthday.

00:44:29.070 --> 00:44:30.070
May God bless.

00:44:30.070 --> 00:44:31.070
Now last but not the least, very important
thing is that the senior people in Sahaja

00:44:31.070 --> 00:44:32.070
Yoga should not be called by their names.

00:44:32.070 --> 00:44:33.070
We can say Uncle or something Uncle Tom, is
to be done.

00:44:33.070 --> 00:44:34.070
It’s very important, and even I’ve heard
some Indian girls calling somebody: ‘John’.

00:44:34.070 --> 00:44:35.070
I said: ‘What?

00:44:35.070 --> 00:44:36.070
He’s like your father.

00:44:36.070 --> 00:44:37.070
How can you call like that?’

00:44:37.070 --> 00:44:38.070
‘Our husbands insist.’

00:44:38.070 --> 00:44:39.070
No, please, call them with some sort of a
uncle and aunty.

00:44:39.070 --> 00:44:40.070
Shouldn’t say like that, it’s not proper,
doesn’t look nice.

00:44:40.070 --> 00:44:41.070
Or address to elders always: ‘Sir’ is
a better idea.

00:44:41.070 --> 00:44:42.070
Shows you have some culture.

00:44:42.070 --> 00:44:43.070
We are not brats, first of all.

00:44:43.070 --> 00:44:44.070
And also we are not people who are hippies,
you see.

00:44:44.070 --> 00:44:45.070
We have to respect the elders.

00:44:45.070 --> 00:44:46.070
Very important, it is that we have to respect
all the elders, that are within you.

00:44:46.070 --> 00:44:47.070
That’s how you will be respected also.

00:44:47.070 --> 00:44:48.070
See to it that those ladies or gentlemen who
are senior people always call them by, either

00:44:48.070 --> 00:44:49.070
‘Mr’ or ‘Uncle’ or ‘Aunt’.

00:44:49.070 --> 00:44:50.070
He was all the time with Me but I somehow
or other sneaked out tying.

00:44:50.070 --> 00:44:51.070
Ah beautiful.

00:44:51.070 --> 00:44:52.070
Suits your hand very well.

00:44:52.070 --> 00:44:53.070
It’s really very [INAUDIBLE] Very very [INAUDIBLE]
All right, so on a very happy note we should

00:44:53.070 --> 00:44:54.070
end up now.

00:44:54.070 --> 00:44:55.070
Feel very sorry that I have to leave you all
here, and there are people waiting, as you

00:44:55.070 --> 00:44:56.070
know in the eastern Asian countries for Me,
counting every minute, so I have to go.

